g  equipment appears to be a new type of  power the flying doesn't last  long though because Dante's gravity  magic forces both Yami and Finn roll to  the ground but Yami manages to land on  his feet  and he also manages to grab Finn Rahl on  his way down  Dante is impressed by Yami's reaction  time and his ability to withstand the  force of Dante's magic without taking on  any damage and this is the point at  which Yami tells us something important  Yami says that during the course of the  last six months or during the course of  the time skip he has learned some new  stuff and he is about to give those new  abilities a test drive we all knew that  just like hasta Yami would surely  receive a massive powerup as a result of  intense training during the time skip  and that is exactly what happened  Yami then proceeds to combine his mana  zone with the dark magic spell black  hole in order to create black moon black  moon is a spell that seems to create a  barrier around the ami and Finn role and  this barrier erases all of the effects  of Dante's magic Dante is again highly  impressed that a vulgar commoner like  Yami could possess such incredible magic  power and it is clear that Dante is  extremely interested in Yami's dark  magic by the way my guess is that Yami's  ability to fly on his own is the result  of him learning to use and control his  mana zone on a completely new level so  I'm going to assume that that's the case  unless we receive some other explanation  at some point in the future Yami tells  fin rot to get out of there and to join  the black Bulls on the sidelines as  Dante decides to use his gravity magic  to launch a massive boulder right at  Yami the boulder looks super scary and  stuff until Yami absolutely annihilates  it with his dark cloaked dimension / he  literally slashes the boulder in half  and Dante remarks that Yami didn't just  slash the rock he actually slashed space  apart this again emphasizes the unique  properties of Yami's dark magic  Yami's magic seems to defy the laws of  nature of this world  cutting through space itself  in this way should not technically be  possible and yet Yami's magic is able to  do exactly that Dante is very excited by  all of this and he decides to charge it  Yami with a sword but if anyone knows  how to kick ass with a sword that would  be our boy Yami and the two majors clash  in a legendary magic infused sword duel  that I'm sure is going to look  absolutely epic in the anime don't get  me wrong it looks epic in the manga as  well but together with animation and  intense music I think it's going to look  even better as long as they don't cheap  out on the budget it's important to  remember that both mages have distinct  strengths in this duel Yami has the  power to react to Dante's moves before  he makes them by combining mana zone  with his key sensing ability and Dante  is able to use his gravity magic to  control the speed of his sword in ways  that no other swordsman would be able to  do during the battle itself dante  reveals to Yami that he is after him or  more accurately he wants Yami because of  his unique magical power presumably  dante wants a demon to take control of  Yami's body so that Yami would then  serve the dark triad as one of its  enforcers  but Yami isn't into dudes like Dante and  being interested in him so Dante's plan  is not gonna fly with our boy ami at  this point Dante says something which i  think is really important  Dante says that Yami is a key that links  this world and the underworld or in  other words this dimension and the  dimension where the demons come from the  fact that Dante refers to Yami as a key  rather than the key implies that there  are more than one keys and all of this  is starting to make a lot of sense if  you think about it we all remember that  dark magic had a unique effect on zag  read the kotodama demon the kind of  effect that no other magic from this  world was able to create as soon as the  unique oth